#document(default_font = "Helvetica", default_size = pt(11), page = { size = "letter" }, margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) })

DRAWINGS IN COLUMNS: a drawing in the text moves to the next column, begins with a column break before it, and is balanced with the text of a continuous section.

#section(columns = { count = 2, gap = pt(18) })[
Alpha sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Alpha sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Alpha sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#shape(position = { width = inch(2), height = pt(60) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape A1 in a column]

Beta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Beta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Beta sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#paragraph(spacing = { before = pt(0), after = pt(0), line = { rule = "exact", value = pt(400) } })[Filler A of 400 points.]

#shape(position = { width = inch(2), height = pt(100) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape A2 moves to the second column]

Gamma sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Gamma sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Gamma sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#group(alignment = "center")[
  #shape(position = { x = inch(0), y = inch(0), width = inch(1.2), height = pt(30) }, fill = "#2563eb", text = { size = pt(9), color = "#ffffff" })[Group A3]
  #shape(position = { x = inch(0.6), y = pt(36), width = inch(1.2), height = pt(24) }, fill = "#059669")
]

Delta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Delta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Delta sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#group(alignment = "right")[
  #shape(position = { x = inch(0), y = inch(0), width = inch(1.2), height = pt(30) }, fill = "#2563eb", text = { size = pt(9), color = "#ffffff" })[Group A4]
  #shape(position = { x = inch(0.6), y = pt(36), width = inch(1.2), height = pt(24) }, fill = "#059669")
]

Epsilon sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Epsilon sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Epsilon sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

]

#section(columns = { count = 2, gap = pt(18) })[
Zeta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Zeta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Zeta sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#shape(position = { width = inch(4), height = pt(50) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape B1 wider than its column]

Eta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Eta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Eta sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#break(type = "column")

#shape(position = { width = inch(2), height = pt(50) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape B2 after a column break]

Theta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Theta sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Theta sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

]

Text before the balanced columns.

#section(columns = { count = 2, gap = pt(18) }, properties = { start = "continuous" })[
Iota sentence fills its column with words that wrap. Iota sentence fills its column with words that wrap.

#shape(position = { width = inch(2), height = pt(70) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape C1 in balanced columns]

Kappa sentence goes down its own column and wraps there. Kappa sentence goes down its own column and wraps there.

#shape(position = { width = inch(2), height = pt(70) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape C2 in balanced columns]

Lambda sentence runs down its own column and wraps there. Lambda sentence runs down its own column and wraps there.

]

#section(columns = { count = 1 }, properties = { start = "continuous" })[
Text after the balanced columns.

#shape(position = { width = inch(2), height = pt(40) }, fill = "#dcfce7", text = { size = pt(10) })[Shape D1 after the columns]

Closing text of the sweep.
